==English==

===Etymology===
{{suffix|milk|y|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈmɪlki/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪlki|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Resembling [[milk]] in [[color]] or [[consistency]].
#* Alexander Pope
#*: pails high foaming with a '''milky''' flood
#* Arbuthnot
#*: '''milky''' juice
# {{context|color science|informal|lang=en}} Of the [[black]] in an [[image]], appearing as dark [[gray]] rather than black.
# {{context|colloquial|lang=en}} [[cowardly|Cowardly]].
#* Shakespeare
#*: Has friendship such a faint and '''milky''' heart?
# {{cx|obsolete|lang=en}} Yielding milk.
#* Roscommon
#*: '''milky''' mothers

